NEWS
------

2026-11-20  Vega Strike Contributors  <maintainers@vega-strike.org>

    * Version 0.1.0 (Modern Engine Compatibility & Universe Expansion):
        - Engine Compatibility & Architecture:
          + Migrated build system from Autotools to modern CMake 3.22+ and multi-target CPack packaging (.tar.xz, .deb, .rpm).
          + Modernized core engine configuration to JSON format (Asset API Version 3):
            engine.json, bindings.json, theme.json, controls.json, config.json.
          + Converted legacy CSV manifests and unit tables to modern JSON:
            master_part_list.json, master_component_list.json, master_asteroid_list.json,
            master_ship_list.json, units.json, ships.json, weapons.json.
          + Full runtime compatibility verified against Vega Strike Engine 0.11.0+.
          + Python 3 runtime support across all base interface rooms and game modules.
          + Replaced legacy fixed-function pipeline with GLSL rendering shaders (programs/ and techniques/).
          + Implemented main menu base interface (bases/main_menu.py, mission/main_menu.mission) and supporting runtime modules for seamless normal startup and campaign launching.

        - Universe & Multi-System Expansion:
          + Expanded Isaac system: Added star Isaac Prime, volcanic world Perdition, terrestrial habitable world Perseverance with surface spaceport, orbital trade station Arachnis Commerce Interchange (Commerce_Center), mined asteroid outpost Ancient Fissure Mining Outpost (MiningBase), and deep-space Refinery.
          + Added Calion system: Warm amber star lighting, volcanic inner planet Scorched Threshold, colony world Aegis Harbor, orbital station Aegis Transfer Concourse (Commerce_Center), and ringed gas giant Calion Major with helium-3 mining base Calion Helium Extraction Hub.
          + Added Nan system: Cool blue star lighting, glacial colony world Frostfall with orbital exchange Frostfall Orbital Exchange (Commerce_Center), asteroid belt installation Nan Outer Belt Refinery (MiningBase), and ringed gas giant Nan Leviathan.
          + Established circular jump network in universe/black_paralysis.xml forming a complete navigational loop: Isaac <-> Calion <-> Nan <-> Isaac.

        - Flyable Ship Roster & Base Dealerships:
          + Restored 5 flyable player vessel classes with authentic 3D models, cockpits, engine thruster meshes, and sound fx:
            Llama (light courier), Plowshare (merchant freighter), Schroedinger (fast patrol interceptor),
            Hyena (medium fighter), and Lancelot (heavy superiority fighter).
          + Populated shipyard inventories and upgrade equipment across commercial centers, refineries, and planetary spaceports.

        - Historical Lore & Asset Preservation:
          + 100% preservation of original soundtrack playlists, sound effects, AI logic, and cockpits.
          + Restored original design documentation and campaign lore (doc/lore/PLANNING.md), original layered splash artwork (resources/artwork/), and Blender XMESH utilities (scripts/tools/).

        - Asset Standardization & Automated Testing:
          + Unwrapped all legacy DDS textures and standardized on PNG and JPG image formats across base rooms, station models, and cockpits.
          + Maintained cubemap background engine compatibility via symlinks (sigma_*.image -> sigma_*.jpg).
          + Added automated test suite for JSON syntax (scripts/test_json_syntax.py), XML/sprite descriptor syntax (scripts/test_xml_syntax.py), and asset cross-reference integrity (scripts/verify_asset_references.py).
          + Added GitHub Actions continuous integration workflow (.github/workflows/validate.yml) running all test suites and CPack packaging builds.

        - Licensing:
          + Upgraded repository license to GNU General Public License Version 3 or later (GPLv3+).

2004-11-24  Daniel Aleksandrow  <dandandaman@users.sourceforge.net>

    * Version 20050902 done.
        In case you didn't notice, the initial release wasn't really much of a
        release at all.  I am now correcting that, with a release that has a
        working autoconf/make system.  It currently will not create anything
        that will work with any released vegastrike binary (or cvs for that
        matter), but the problems preventing this are known, and fixes are only
        to be implemented in the main tree.
        Stil both 100% cruft and content free ;-)
    	
        Known Issues:
          + The armour error you will get upon loading the data set is due to
            the fact that the default (non existant) craft you fly has a mass
            of 0.  A units.csv file will fix this.
          + The make system will not work due to non-existant directories.

2004-11-24  Daniel Aleksandrow  <dandandaman@users.sourceforge.net>

